# gh-image — the ONE build bin/gh-attach will run. Parsed as data (never sourced).
#   version <tag>        the upstream tag, drogers0/gh-image (MIT); also the -X main.version the build stamps
#   commit  <sha>        the commit that was audited (2026-11-05) and that setup/install/install-gh-image.sh BUILDS:
#                        fetched by this full sha, never by a tag name or a release asset
#   source  <https>      where install-gh-image.sh fetches it from; it refuses any other
#   go      <toolchain>  the Go toolchain the hash below was measured with (go env GOVERSION); another one is refused
#   sha256 <os-arch> <hex>  checksum of the binary THAT BUILD produces on <os-arch> (kooky, the default tags; not hbd)
# The build: CGO_ENABLED=0 GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly (go.sum of the commit decides every module) GOTOOLCHAIN=local, `go build
# -trimpath -buildvcs=false -ldflags "-s -w -X main.version=<version without v>"`, in an environment of its own.
# Changing a line here is a change of the security boundary: re-audit the new commit first
# (setup/briefs/gh-image-upload-tool.md, § Audit; docs/gh-attach.md).
# A platform with no sha256 row is unsupported: build it there twice, check both hashes are equal, then add the row.
# The release binary of v1.4.1 (sha256 f566ed6e…, the pin before 2026-11-06) is NOT what this build produces
# (see docs/gh-attach.md): bin/gh-attach refuses it.
version v1.4.1
commit ca57d96dd4ac72bae5c8264a244116bd17f96ce8
source https://github.com/drogers0/gh-image
go go1.27.3
sha256 darwin-arm64 d308dfe11a8e329fdd7fc3b7fb02f700f8708f27ccf6992b9784f00236caa5b0
